# A rownum parameter must plan the run-time row lookup with today's filter kept as its fallback child.

admin 'create table test::t28 { id: int4, a: int4 }'
---
> +---------+-------------+---------+-----------+
> |   id    |  namespace  |  table  |  created  |
> +---------+-------------+---------+-----------+
> |  16388  |    test     |   t28   |   true    |
> +---------+-------------+---------+-----------+
>

query 'CALL rql::explain("from test::t28 filter {rownum == $1}")'
